                <pb facs="0237" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg141"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Situation worse. It is possible we may be besieged in Pekin, with railways and
                    telegraphs cut. In that case I ask, as my colleagues are doing, that necessary
                    instructions be given Admiral concert with other chiefs of squadron at Taku to
                    take measures warranted by the situation to eventually deliver Pekin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
